l square\n- Attacks White's developed knight on c3\n- Controls key central squares (d2, f2, c5, d6)\n- Maintains flexibility for Black's development\n- Puts immediate pressure on White\n\n**Reason:**\nN: f6-e4 is the strongest move because it actively centralizes the knight while creating immediate threats. The knight on e4 is difficult to dislodge and gives Black excellent control of the center. This forcing move puts White on the defensive and allows Black to maintain the initiative while completing development.\n\n**Answer:** N: f6-e4"}
