ck to the white king on e1\n- Simultaneously attacks the rook on h1\n- White must respond to the check by moving the king\n- Then I capture the rook on h1, winning significant material (rook worth ~5 points)\n\nThis is a game-winning tactical blow.\n\nReason: N: e4-f2 is a royal fork that checks the white king on e1 while simultaneously attacking the rook on h1. White must respond to the check, after which I win the rook, gaining a decisive material advantage of approximately 5 points (a full rook). This tactical strike should lead to a winning position.\n\nAnswer: N: e4-f2"}
